      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Oak Creek runs south of Ellsworth, joining the Smoky Hill River southeast of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellsworth%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s heritage tourism centers on its 19th‑century cattle‑town past, highlighted by annual cattle drives down Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellsworth%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Hodgden House Museum Complex, built in 1873, houses a rare wooden Union Pacific caboose and the town’s oldest jail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlindsborg.com/ellsworth",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Preisker Park showcases stone bridges and a bandshell that hosts local entertainment, reflecting the town’s historic charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
